* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* eviVLP: hand-curated parameters for the AMINOXYL (nitroxide) RADICAL  >N-O.
*
* WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
*   CGenFF has no atom type for a persistent aminoxyl radical, in any release
*   (checked v4.6 and v5.0). The two types it reaches for are both wrong:
*     NG2O1 / OG2N1  -> nitro group (R-NO2), not >N-O.
*     NG301 / OG312  -> OG312 is "anionic alcohol oxygen" (alkoxide). The
*                       CGenFF program picks this when the input structure
*                       draws the radical as the N(+)-O(-) zwitterion, which
*                       is what Open Babel writes. It then assigns a charge
*                       near -0.66 to the oxygen and leaves the residue with
*                       a spurious net -1.
*     NG301 / OG311  -> v5.0 added these, but as an N-HYDROXYLAMINE: the bond
*                       is 1.4104 A and it carries an N-O-H angle term. The
*                       aminoxyl N-O is ~1.26 A and has no hydrogen.
*   So the radical must be typed by hand and these terms must override the
*   release values. Load this file AFTER par_GUI.prm so it wins.
*
* TYPING CONVENTION
*   radical N -> NG301   (tertiary aliphatic amine N; vdW eps -0.0350 Rmin/2 2.00)
*   radical O -> OG311   (methanol/ethanol O; vdW eps -0.1921 Rmin/2 1.7650)
*                NO hydrogen is bonded to this oxygen.
*   OG311 is used purely to borrow a reasonable oxygen vdW. The bonded terms
*   below replace the hydroxyl geometry with nitroxide geometry.
*
* PROVENANCE  (confirmed)
*   D. Sezer, J. H. Freed and B. Roux, J. Phys. Chem. B 2008, 112, 5755-5767.
*   Lumata et al., J. Mater. Chem. B 2024, 12, 3273-3281 cites this as ref 71
*   and its methods state the model used "the CHARMM all-atom force field and
*   TEMPO parameters from Sezer et al., supplemented by the CGenFF force
*   field" (refs 72/73 being Vanommeslaeghe/MacKerell, J. Chem. Inf. Model.
*   2012, 52, 3155-3168 and 3144-3154). The three terms below annotated
*   "Roux" are carried verbatim from extra.prm in the 2023 production runs.
*   Everything else is CGenFF-by-analogy, retyped OG312 -> OG311.
*
* AS-SIMULATED RECORD
*   These values, and the charges in the table below, are the ones actually
*   used in the 2023 runs. Verified against RESI LYT (T158K arm) and RESI YMT
*   (Y139 arm) in top_all27_prot_na_CBD.inp, and against the production
*   structure T158K_new.psf, segment PA1 residue 158, where N7 carries
*   +0.167 and O3 carries -0.379.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

BONDS
!     i      j        Kb        b0
NG301  OG311   485.17     1.2640 ! nitroxide N-O, Roux. REPLACES the CGenFF v5.0
                                 ! hydroxylamine value 234.14 / 1.4104
CG301  NG301   200.00     1.4500 ! ***** , from CG321 NG301, penalty= 12

ANGLES
!     i      j      k      Ktheta  Theta0
CG301  NG301  CG301    38.60    119.00 ! nitroxide, Roux. Near-planar N, not 112
CG301  NG301  OG311    45.12    115.52 ! nitroxide, Roux
CG321  CG301  NG301    57.00    107.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301, penalty= 12
CG331  CG301  NG301    43.70    112.20 ! ***** , from CG331 CG321 NG311, penalty= 12.6

DIHEDRALS
!     i      j      k      l         Kchi   n   delta
CG321  CG301  NG301  OG311      1.4200  1   180.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
CG321  CG301  NG301  OG311      0.8200  2     0.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
CG321  CG301  NG301  OG311      1.0200  3     0.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
CG331  CG301  NG301  OG311      1.4200  1   180.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
CG331  CG301  NG301  OG311      0.8200  2     0.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
CG331  CG301  NG301  OG311      1.0200  3     0.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
CG321  CG301  NG301  CG301      1.4200  1   180.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
CG321  CG301  NG301  CG301      0.8200  2     0.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
CG321  CG301  NG301  CG301      1.0200  3     0.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
CG331  CG301  NG301  CG301      1.4200  1   180.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
CG331  CG301  NG301  CG301      0.8200  2     0.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
CG331  CG301  NG301  CG301      1.0200  3     0.00 ! ***** , from CG321 CG321 NG301 CG321
NG301  CG301  CG321  HGA2       0.1600  3     0.00 ! ***** , from NG301 CG321 CG321 HGA2
NG301  CG301  CG331  HGA3       0.1600  3     0.00 ! ***** , from NG311 CG321 CG331 HGA3

IMPROPERS
! none. The aminoxyl N is left to the angle terms above; no out-of-plane
! restraint was used in the 2023 runs.

! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! PARTIAL CHARGES for the 2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidin-1-oxyl (TEMPO) cage,
! in the machine-readable form apply_charge_overrides.py reads. NAMD ignores
! comment lines, so this one file is both the loadable parameter set and the
! charge record. Charges live in the PSF, so these are applied to the stream
! file BEFORE psfgen, via the "Apply charge overrides" button.
!
! WHY THE WHOLE CAGE IS LISTED, not just N and O: CGenFF reads the bare N-O as
! an ALKOXIDE (oxygen typed OG312, "anionic alcohol oxygen"), so it gives the
! group a formal charge of -1. Correcting that is a whole electron, and a whole
! electron cannot be absorbed by nudging one or two atoms - it has to be taken
! up by replacing every charge in the group. Listing only N and O leaves ~1 e
! to redistribute, which the script refuses.
!
! TARGET IS +1, AND IT IS NOT THE RADICAL. The aminoxyl is a neutral radical;
! the N-O pair sums to -0.2120, a dipole inside a neutral group. The +1 is the
! protonated secondary amine of the 4-amino-TEMPO linker, which is an ammonium
! (nitrogen with four bonds, type NG3P2) at pH 7. Radical character and formal
! charge are independent: TEMPO's own oxidation product, the oxoammonium cation
! TEMPO+, is a charged radical-derived species. If the linker amine is drawn
! NEUTRAL the residue is 0, not +1, and the script will say so.
!
! ATOM NAMES below are whatever CGenFF assigned in the most recent run. CGenFF
! names atoms from the order they appear in the upload, so every re-run
! renumbers them and these names go stale. Do NOT edit them by hand - run
!
!     python3 map_override_atoms.py nad.str nitroxide_overrides.prm
!
! after each CGenFF import. That script resolves each `role=` tag below from the
! residue's own BOND records and rewrites only the name column; the types,
! charges and target are the published values and it never touches them.
! Nothing is renamed in the molecule itself - the atoms keep CGenFF's names,
! which the .pdb, the patch and IC_naa all depend on.
!
! The recognising-a-nitroxide logic lives in map_override_atoms.py, here in the
! case study, NOT in the GUI. The GUI's apply_charge_overrides.py addresses
! atoms by name and knows no chemistry, so it serves any small molecule. A
! different molecule CGenFF cannot type needs its own small mapper, or its
! names written out by hand.
!
! Published 2023 names (RESI LYT / RESI YMT), for the record, in role order:
!   N7, O3, C19/C25, C20/C24, C21/C22/C26/C27, C23, C28
!
! @CHARGES  residue=NAA  target=+1
! N1    NG301  +0.167 ! role=radical_N   the N bonded to a terminal O
! O1    OG311  -0.379 ! role=radical_O   that O, no hydrogen (CGenFF types it OG312)
! C2    CG301  +0.284 ! role=alpha_C     quaternary carbon alpha to N
! C7    CG301  +0.284 ! role=alpha_C     quaternary carbon alpha to N
! C1    CG321  -0.237 ! role=ring_CH2    ring CH2 (its H stay at +0.090)
! C6    CG321  -0.237 ! role=ring_CH2    ring CH2
! C4    CG331  -0.300 ! role=methyl_C    gem-dimethyl (its H stay at +0.090)
! C5    CG331  -0.300 ! role=methyl_C    gem-dimethyl
! C8    CG331  -0.300 ! role=methyl_C    gem-dimethyl
! C9    CG331  -0.300 ! role=methyl_C    gem-dimethyl
! C3    CG314  +0.248 ! role=ring_C_sub  the 4-position carbon, bearing the linker
! @BALANCE  C10 ! role=linker_C1
! @END
!
! @BALANCE takes the first substituent carbon past the 4-position, which absorbs
! the small remainder
! (+0.101 against the published values). Never balance onto the protein
! backbone: those atoms must keep their standard CHARMM36 LYS/TYR charges for
! the cross-force-field junction to behave.
!
! The cage alone - N, O, both alpha carbons, both ring CH2, four methyls and
! all their hydrogens, i.e. everything except C23 and its substituent - sums to
! +0.1220. It is deliberately NOT a neutral group on its own.
!
! Source: D. Sezer, J. H. Freed and B. Roux, J. Phys. Chem. B 2008, 112,
! 5755-5767, cited as ref 71 in Lumata et al., J. Mater. Chem. B 2024, 12,
! 3273-3281, whose methods state the model used "the CHARMM all-atom force
! field and TEMPO parameters from Sezer et al., supplemented by the CGenFF
! force field".
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

END
